This is AMON-SENSS, software for scalable detection of DDoS attacks and
creation of signatures for attack filtering. Signatures and alerts are
exported in real time into alerts.txt file. You will soon discover when
you run this tool that there are many attacks that get detected. This is
an unfortunate fact -- today's traffic is often one-way and has many
anomalies that AMON-SENSS picks up.

==== NOTES FOR EVALUATORS ===

Please allocate an XDC on SPHERE, clone AMON-SENSS repo, then within it run

git checkout example1
git pull

After that run

/share/startexp -n amonsess -t topology.model

Once the experiment is allocated and attached SSH to the node by doing

ssh a

Clone the repo again on that node, and run

git checkout example1
git pull

Then run

bash install

==== RUNNING ====

To check claim run

bash claim1.sh

Once the code indicates that it has finished press CTRL-C to exit.

Then run

perl sum_alerts alerts.txt

and it should print out one attack detected with the signature of UDP flood.

